course: dictionary
lesson: 15409
title: Spouting: a word with three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Spouting is a good example. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer means. «The whale was spouting water high into the air.» Here the water is shooting out in a strong stream, like a fountain.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Stop spouting nonsense, Tom.» Nobody is watching water here. Spouting means talking a lot, without thinking, and it sounds rude or annoyed. Ask yourself: would this sentence make sense with a different meaning?
explain: Sometimes the word comes from another country. In Australia and New Zealand, a spouting is the gutter along the edge of a roof. «Clean the leaves out of the spouting before the rain.» The clue is the word leaves: a gutter catches the leaves and rainwater, so spouting must mean the gutter.
fact: Spouting is a form of the verb spout, which means to pour or shoot out in a strong stream.
fact: Whales are seen spouting when they breathe out through their blowholes.
fact: Volcanoes and geysers can spout water or lava.
fact: «Spouting off» means talking too much or showing off what you think.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a spouting is the gutter on a roof that collects rainwater.
exercise: «The whale was spouting water high into the air.» What is spouting doing here? | *Pouring out in a strong stream | Swimming very slowly | Hiding from the boats | Sleeping quietly under the sea
exercise: «Stop spouting nonsense, Tom.» What does spouting suggest? | Cleaning the kitchen floor | Running very fast | Singing a happy song | *Talking a lot without thinking
exercise: An Aussie mate says, «Clean the leaves out of the spouting before the rain.» What is the spouting? | A wooden fence post | A type of fish that lives in rivers | *A gutter along a roof that collects rainwater | A kind of tall tree
test: «The volcano was spouting hot lava into the sky.» What does spouting mean here? | Very quiet | *Shooting out in a strong stream | Growing slowly | Sleeping
test: «Dad says Ella is spouting off about the game again.» What does spouting off mean? | Pouring out rain | Swimming fast | Cleaning the windows | *Talking too much and showing off
exam: «The whale was spouting, and a cloud of mist rose from the sea.» Which clue shows that spouting means breathing out water? | *A cloud of mist rising from the sea | A roof full of leaves | Hot lava | The word nonsense
